---
import ContentPage from "@/layouts/ContentPage.astro";
---
<ContentPage
  title="Cookie Policy | SpedCentral"
  description="What cookies SpedCentral uses today, and how we'll handle future analytics or advertising cookies."
  heading="Cookie Policy"
  lastUpdated="July 27, 2026"
>
  <p>
    A cookie is a small text file a website stores in your browser to remember information between visits. Here's
    what SpedCentral actually uses today.
  </p>

  <h2>What we use right now</h2>
  <p>
    SpedCentral currently uses only <strong>strictly necessary</strong> cookies/local storage required for the Site
    to function -- for example, remembering your search when you navigate between pages. We do not currently use
    advertising cookies, and we do not currently run third-party analytics or ad-tracking scripts.
  </p>

  <h2>What changes when we add analytics or advertising</h2>
  <p>
    As SpedCentral grows, we plan to add privacy-respecting analytics (to understand which pages are useful) and
    may run affiliate or advertising partnerships that use cookies. Before we do, we'll update this policy and add
    a cookie consent banner so you can accept or decline non-essential cookies -- this section will be updated the
    day that happens, and the "Last updated" date above will change.
  </p>

  <h2>Controlling cookies in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    You can block or delete cookies through your browser settings at any time. Blocking strictly necessary cookies
    may affect how parts of the Site function (like search filters resetting between pages).
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party sites</h2>
  <p>
    Links to provider websites, affiliate purchase pages, and payment processors take you off SpedCentral to sites
    with their own cookie practices, which this policy doesn't cover.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@spedcentral.com">hello@spedcentral.com</a> with any questions about this policy.</p>
</ContentPage>
